Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the XML module
=========================================

qore-xml-module ships the native XML module, all 17 associated Qore modules
as sources and compiled qmods, compiler metadata, provider catalogs and schemas,
and soaputil/webdav-server. The doc package supplies all 18 API references.
Debhelper generates matching debug symbols for the native and AOT modules.

Dependencies and source preparation
----------------------------------

Qualification targets Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 with the packaged Qore 3.0 SDK.
Other releases and architectures require their own SDK and qualification.
Cross builds are rejected because native Qore tools run during compilation.

The module requires its patched libxml2 2.15.4 for namespace, schema and value
handling. The package uses a private static build with hidden symbols and
ships no replacement system libxml2 library. All existing upstream fixes in
cmake/QoreXmlLibXml2.cmake are retained. fast_float 8.3.0 is also private.
Updates to these bundled components require security review and rebuilding
this package; an update of the system libxml2 package does not update them.

The multi-component source package includes libxml2 in an orig-libxml2 tarball.
Download the URL in debian/vendor-sources.json during source preparation, then
run debian/repack-libxml2.py; it checks the pinned SHA256 and removes test/result
fixtures following the distribution's libxml2 repack. Binary builds use that
local source component with FetchContent downloads disabled.

The main orig excludes prebuilt Java interoperability JARs and two
generated Salesforce WSDLs listed in Files-Excluded. The Salesforce files
carry no redistribution license; their original-byte regression case skips
explicitly when they are absent. Live tests use a user-supplied WSDL. The
unneeded RFC 2392 reference text is also excluded because its terms are not
DFSG-free. The remaining Qore tests run without Java. UN/CEFACT schemas
are redistributed unchanged under the notices retained in every schema;
their modification restrictions preclude inclusion in Debian main. This PPA
package includes them to preserve CargoXmlDataProvider functionality. No
IATA-licensed Cargo-XML toolkit is included.

Use a fresh version for each changed upload. From a clean committed checkout,
prepare the main orig and the separately downloaded libxml2 component:

    version=$(dpkg-parsechangelog -SVersion)
    upstream=${version%-*}
    work=$(realpath ../xml-package-work)
    mkdir -p "$work"
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-xml-module-$upstream/" HEAD -- \
        . ':!debian' ':!test/wsdl-interop/oracle/*.jar' \
        ':!test/wsdl-interop/axis-peer/jars/*.jar' \
        ':!test/wsdl-interop/cxf-peer/jars/*.jar' \
        ':!test/enterprise.wsdl' ':!test/partner.wsdl' \
        ':!test/wsdl-interop/normative/rfc2392.txt' | xz > \
        "$work/qore-xml-module_$upstream.orig.tar.xz"
    debian/repack-libxml2.py /path/to/libxml2-2.15.4.tar.xz "$work"
    tar -xf "$work/qore-xml-module_$upstream.orig.tar.xz" -C "$work"
    tree="$work/qore-xml-module-$upstream"
    cp -a debian "$tree/"
    mkdir "$tree/libxml2"
    tar -xf "$work/qore-xml-module_$upstream.orig-libxml2.tar.xz" \
        --strip-components=1 -C "$tree/libxml2"
    cd "$tree"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Build and qualify
-----------------

Install debian/control's Build-Depends in an isolated native environment,
extract the .dsc into a clean directory, then build unprivileged with network
access disabled using dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc. -B builds runtime/debug
only and -A builds documentation. The nodoc profile omits the doc package;
nodoc in DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS suppresses documentation generation. Do not use
nocheck for the full qualification build or installed tests. Reproducibility
and profile-only rebuilds may use nocheck after the full test run passes.

The build enables AOT, disables source-tree qmod symlinks and honors noopt.
QCC_JOBS=1 fixes the codegen partition count independently of CPU count and
transient GNU make jobserver load; independent modules still build in parallel.
QCC_SPLIT_THRESHOLD is cleared so host compiler tuning does not affect builds.
Tests load the built modules and packaged standard library only, with no qlib
source fallback. Compiler metadata and source locations survive stripping
through the preserve-aot-metadata.py wrapper copied from Qore. Its real-ELF
unit tests run during builds. dwz is disabled for the runtime package because
it does not support all LLVM DWARF forms; matching debug packages are retained.
Runtime dependencies include the interpreter and libqore SONAME package at
least as new as the SDK used for compilation, plus dh_shlibdeps dependencies.
The architecture-specific runtime is not marked Multi-Arch: same.

Package tests run all Qore .qtest suites and four native regression probes,
validate complete provider translations, and exercise the WebDAV CLI over
loopback HTTP including shutdown. process and litmus are build/test-only
dependencies: the WebDAV compliance test skips gracefully when process is
absent during ordinary source testing and fails if compliance is required.
Salesforce account tests skip without credentials; no account credentials
are provided during packaging. Java/lxml interoperability and live Salesforce
qualification require separate configured environments.

Installed autopkgtests verify all 17 compiled module paths, run the suites
without source modules available, and compile a fresh executable exercising
named XML arguments. Retain exact source/package hashes, dependency inventories
and logs. Also check Lintian, hardening, AOT trailers, runtime install without
SDK, docs/debug coinstallation, dpkg -V, purge/reinstall and reproducibility
in distinct build directories. PPA testing is separate from final release.
